│   ├── schema.sql
│   └── analysis_queries.sql
│
├── 📂 src/
│   ├── data_cleaning.py
│   ├── data_analysis.py
│   ├── database.py
│   └── visualizations.py
│
├── 📂 notebooks/
│   └── sales_analysis.ipynb
│
└── 📂 tests/
    └── test_analytics.py
⚙️ Installation
1️⃣ Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/sales-performance-analytics.git
cd sales-performance-analytics
2️⃣ Create Virtual Environment
python -m venv venv
3️⃣ Activate Environment

Windows:

venv\Scripts\activate

Mac/Linux:

source venv/bin/activate
4️⃣ Install Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
📊 Generate Dataset
python generate_dataset.py
🗄️ MySQL Setup

Configure your MySQL credentials in .env.

Then run:

python -c "from src.database import init_database, load_csv_to_mysql; init_database(); load_csv_to_mysql()"
▶️ Run Dashboard
streamlit run app.py

🌐 Open in your browser:

http://localhost:8501
🧪 Run Tests
python run_tests.py

Or:

pytest -v tests/test_analytics.py
💡 Business Insights

The dashboard dynamically identifies:

🏆 Best-performing region
📦 Top-selling products
💰 Most profitable products
🏷️ Best-performing categories
📉 Low-performing products
📈 Sales growth
💹 Profit margin
🎯 Discount impact

⚠️ Limitations

🔹 Dataset is synthetic
🔹 Pricing and costs are simulated
🔹 MySQL can be used optionally with CSV fallback

